    "body": "`WarmupLR`, `WarmupDecayLR` and `WarmupCosineLR` raise `ValueError: warmup_num_steps must be a positive integer, got 0` since 0.19.3. HF Trainer writes 0 into `\"warmup_num_steps\": \"auto\"` when no warmup is set, so those runs fail at startup on transformers before 5.18 (5.18 works around it with `max(1, ...)` in huggingface/transformers#48640). HodeTech/ForgeLM#502 hit this.\n\n**Cause:** #8126 added a `<= 0` check. Before it, 0 was valid and `max(2, warmup_num_steps)` clamped it to 2, the same as 1.\n\n**Fix:** Reject only negative values in both checks, so 0 behaves as before. `None` and negative values still raise.\n\n**Test:** New `test_warmup_schedulers_accept_zero_warmup_num_steps` checks that 0 gives the same LRs as 2 for all three schedulers. It fails on master with that ValueError and passes after. `test_lr_schedulers.py` passes (91 tests, CPU). yapf and flake8 are clean.\n",
    "changed_files": 2,
    "closed_at": null,
